#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:5
msgid ""
"The configuration options in `bitmapPseudoMerge.*` are considered "
"EXPERIMENTAL and may be subject to change or be removed entirely in the "
"future. For more information about the pseudo-merge bitmap feature, see the "
"\"Pseudo-merge bitmaps\" section of linkgit:gitpacking[7]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "bitmapPseudoMerge.<name>.pattern"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:12
msgid ""
"Regular expression used to match reference names. Commits pointed to by "
"references matching this pattern (and meeting the below criteria, like "
"`bitmapPseudoMerge.<name>.sampleRate` and "
"`bitmapPseudoMerge.<name>.threshold`) will be considered for inclusion in a "
"pseudo-merge bitmap."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:16
msgid ""
"Commits are grouped into pseudo-merge groups based on whether or not any "
"reference(s) that point at a given commit match the pattern, which is an "
"extended regular expression."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:22
msgid ""
"Within a pseudo-merge group, commits may be further grouped into sub-groups "
"based on the capture groups in the pattern. These sub-groupings are formed "
"from the regular expressions by concatenating any capture groups from the "
"regular expression, with a '-' dash in between."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:29
msgid ""
"For example, if the pattern is `refs/tags/`, then all tags (provided they "
"meet the below criteria) will be considered candidates for the same "
"pseudo-merge group. However, if the pattern is instead "
"`refs/remotes/([0-9])+/tags/`, then tags from different remotes will be "
"grouped into separate pseudo-merge groups, based on the remote number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "bitmapPseudoMerge.<name>.decay"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:35
msgid ""
"Determines the rate at which consecutive pseudo-merge bitmap groups decrease "
"in size. Must be non-negative. This parameter can be thought of as `k` in "
"the function `f(n) = C * n^-k`, where `f(n)` is the size of the `n`th group."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:41
msgid ""
"Setting the decay rate equal to `0` will cause all groups to be the same "
"size. Setting the decay rate equal to `1` will cause the `n`th group to be "
"`1/n` the size of the initial group.  Higher values of the decay rate cause "
"consecutive groups to shrink at an increasing rate.  The default is `1`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:46
msgid ""
"If all groups are the same size, it is possible that groups containing newer "
"commits will be able to be used less often than earlier groups, since it is "
"more likely that the references pointing at newer commits will be updated "
"more often than a reference pointing at an old commit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "bitmapPseudoMerge.<name>.sampleRate"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:52
msgid ""
"Determines the proportion of non-bitmapped commits (among reference tips) "
"which are selected for inclusion in an unstable pseudo-merge bitmap. Must be "
"between `0` and `1` (inclusive). The default is `1`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "bitmapPseudoMerge.<name>.threshold"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:58
msgid ""
"Determines the minimum age of non-bitmapped commits (among reference tips, "
"as above) which are candidates for inclusion in an unstable pseudo-merge "
"bitmap. The default is `1.week.ago`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "bitmapPseudoMerge.<name>.maxMerges"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:62
msgid ""
"Determines the maximum number of pseudo-merge commits among which commits "
"may be distributed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:67
msgid ""
"For pseudo-merge groups whose pattern does not contain any capture groups, "
"this setting is applied for all commits matching the regular expression. For "
"patterns that have one or more capture groups, this setting is applied for "
"each distinct capture group."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:73
msgid ""
"For example, if your capture group is `refs/tags/`, then this setting will "
"distribute all tags into a maximum of `maxMerges` pseudo-merge "
"commits. However, if your capture group is, say, "
"`refs/remotes/([0-9]+)/tags/`, then this setting will be applied to each "
"remote's set of tags individually."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:75
msgid "Must be non-negative. The default value is 64."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "bitmapPseudoMerge.<name>.stableThreshold"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:82
msgid ""
"Determines the minimum age of commits (among reference tips, as above, "
"however stable commits are still considered candidates even when they have "
"been covered by a bitmap) which are candidates for a stable a pseudo-merge "
"bitmap. The default is `1.month.ago`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:88
msgid ""
"Setting this threshold to a smaller value (e.g., 1.week.ago) will cause more "
"stable groups to be generated (which impose a one-time generation cost) but "
"those groups will likely become stale over time. Using a larger value incurs "
"the opposite penalty (fewer stable groups which are more useful)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "bitmapPseudoMerge.<name>.stableSize"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/config/bitmap-pseudo-merge.txt:91
msgid ""
"Determines the size (in number of commits) of a stable psuedo-merge "
"bitmap. The default is `512`."
msgstr ""
